## Report: `DET.NAV.DEPTH` handbook page

Replaced the harness bootstrap stub with a full PDCA handbook page aligned to `det-nav-depth.check.js` and sibling rule pages (`det-nav-dedup`, `det-nav-breadcrumb`).

### Written content

**Title:** Global navigation depth

**Summary:** Global primary nav outside `main` stays at top level + one flyout tier (`list_depth ≤ 2`); deeper IA belongs in **Ksr** sidebar/offcanvas or an explicit mega-menu (≤ 4 tiers).

**Sections:**
- **Purpose** — PDCA framing; root selectors (`nav.fs-primary-nav-global`, `nav.landing-nav`, **Kpn**); depth caps (2 standard / 4 mega); exclusions (theme menus); **Ksr** is not a global-nav root
- **Passing signals** — shallow **Kpn** / `landing-nav`, `fs-nav-dropdown` single tier, deep trees in **Ksr**
- **Failing signals** — `nested-flyout-depth`, `mega-depth-exceeded`, co-fail patterns with dedup/context burden
- **Before example** — `landing-header` + nested `<ul>` chain (depth 4) using `landing-nav-link`, `fs-brand`, `fs-landing-main`, `forge-support`
- **After example** — **Kpn** with `fs-primary-nav-global-inner`, `fs-nav-dropdown` / `__trigger` / `__panel-inner` / `__link`, plus **Ksr** `forge-sidebar` with `nav-scroll`, `nav-section-label`, `nav-link`
- **Evidence and remediation** — `collectNavDepthReport`, evidence tokens, 6-step fix order
- **Related rules** — DEDUP, BREADCRUMB, FOCUS_ORDER, CONTEXT.BURDEN, PAGE.MODE, CHROME.BOUNDARY

